  "cases": [
    "9 SQL/HTTP: every current route has reviewed guards and private routes reject missing credentials",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: every route with resource parameters preserves the second account under owner spoofing",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: backups exclude credentials and cannot export the other account through query or body",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: endpoint ownership cannot be stolen concurrently by a second account",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: subscription response excludes capability and keys, deletion is account scoped",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: provider 404 and 410 retire only the expired subscription",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: explicit transient provider refusal has one bounded retry and accurate acceptance count",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: test push distinguishes attempted devices from provider acceptance",
    "9 SQL: cancelled and replaced rest reminders cannot consume the latest durable event",
    "9 SQL: concurrent schedules keep one durable rest event and one private provider message",
    "9 SQL/lifecycle: closing pauses sends while an accepted HTTP request can persist its reminder for restart",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: an acknowledged rest cancellation is idempotent, account scoped and survives restart",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: delayed cancellation of an old generation cannot cancel its replacement",
    "9 SQL/processes: simultaneous restoration by two backends consumes a rest reminder once",
    "9 SQL/processes: creatine stages are claimed once across two independent application processes",
    "9 SQL/processes: reengagement daily claim survives competing processes and restart",
    "9 SQL/processes: abrupt crash before provider acceptance rolls back the rest claim for restart",
    "9 SQL: disabled category and recorded dose prevent creatine messages",
    "9 SQL: stale reminders are discarded on restart and forged reminder owner never receives exercise data",
    "9 SQL: logout removal during a multi-device send prevents the removed device attempt",
    "9 SQL/HTTP: login repetition is bounded under concurrency with generic credentials failures",
    "9 SQL/auth: concurrent credential updates cannot revoke the winning replacement token a second time",
    "9 time: CDMX midnight, Sunday, week, month and year boundaries preserve stage/date semantics"
